  "name": "Gambuh (Balinese court dance-drama ensemble)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Oldest surviving Balinese dance-drama, enacting Panji tales in Kawi dialogue and song, and a source of much later Balinese dance and gamelan repertoire. Its ensemble is led by several very long suling gambuh flutes and a rebab, with paired kendang, kajar and small gongs and cymbals; Batuan and Pedungan are among the villages that keep it.",
